                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Tough call[/h1]\n\nI have had this game on my wishlist since 2019, simply because I loved the concept. Back then there weren't many screenshots, it was mostly concept art or just imagination.\nBut I liked what I saw and I was intrigued by how it would play out. \n\nSo I wishlisted the game and waited. \nNot many news about the game came out and I slightly expected it to disappear into the void forever.\n\nIt's been three years since that day and today I got a notification saying it released.\nTo be honest, I stopped following any news after two years.\n\nInstantly bought it and well.\n\n[b]I do not recommend this game.[/b]\n\n[b]Con's:[/b]\n🞨 Very repetitive, same scenarios throughout the city.\n🞨 Camera movement feels slow and the audiop of it doesn't always loop properly.\n🞨 AI feels unrealistic\n\n[b]Pro's[/b]\n✓ Interesting concept.\n✓ Runs smoothly \n✓ Good pricing\n✓ More to do than I expected, tho sadly not enough.\n(Sometimes one cam has like 7 different events, while one has none)\n\nAll in all, it's not a bad game, it's just [i]boring[/i].\nI know with the price and all it's not supposed to be breathtaking, but I expected at least [i]something to keep me occupied more than 11 minutes.[/i]\n\nEmergency vehicles just disappear once the issue is \"resolved\", reading through drug dealers personal feels tells me [u]nothing[/u]. It's just empty. And empty world with randomly generated events.\n\nI thought this would be nice to play to pass the time; calming down, something you just put on and enjoy.\nBut even that I can't do.\n\nI like the concept, I really do.\nI waited over [b]3 years[/b] and I am just not entertained. I am not disappointed either tho, since it [b]did[/b] release after all.\n\nSadly, I can [u]not[/u] recommend this game.\n\n[h1]2/10[/h1]\n[i](For the fact that yes, it did infact release and it's not absolute trash.[/i]",
                        "timestamp_created": 1660313115,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1660313219,
